 \begin{equation*}
 \min\left\{\int_{\Omega}f\left(x, Dv(x)\right)dx\,:\,v\in
 \mathcal{K}_{\phi}(\bar{\Omega})\supset\phi\right\},
 \end{equation*}
 where the convex integrand $f$ exhibits only minimal growth conditions with respect to the gradient and the domain variable, and is required to be quasi-convex rather than $C^2$ smooth.  As a result, we establish that the regular points of the solution possess higher regularity, according to the equation's characteristics, even when the equation is fully degenerate ($p>1$).  This result is established in a general setting and includes cases with non-standard growth conditions, as well as the biphasic scenario, where we obtain $C^{1,\sigma}(\Omega)$ regularity for the obstacle problem.  However, due to potential singularities in solutions to the equation, we are unable to establish further regularity for the obstacle problem's solution.
